## 5. Entity lifecycle callbacks / JPA listeners / auditing

Only one lifecycle callback exists; there are NO `@EntityListeners`, no JPA auditing, no `@PreUpdate`/`@PostPersist`.

`Owner.onCreate()` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`:
```java
143    @PrePersist
144    protected void onCreate() {
145        this.registrationDate = BusinessDays.effectiveRegistrationDate(this.registrationDate);
146    }
```
This is a `@PrePersist` backstop that re-applies the "default-to-now, then roll to business day" policy at flush time (idempotent, so the already-adjusted value from the controller is unchanged). Entity validation constraints (`Owner`/`Person`): `@NotEmpty` on firstName, lastName (Person lines 32,36), address, city (Owner 41,45); `@NotEmpty @Pattern(regexp="^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$")` on telephone (Owner 49-50); `@Email` on email (Owner 54). Id is `@GeneratedValue(IDENTITY)` (`BaseEntity` lines 33-34).

## 6. Spring Security / authorization

Method-level: `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` on `addOwner` (controller line 83). `@roles` resolves to the `Roles` component — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/Roles.java` line 8: `OWNER_ADMIN = "ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN"`, so effectively requires authority `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`.

Two mutually exclusive filter chains, toggled by `petclinic.security.enable`:
- `BasicAuthenticationConfig` (`...enable=true`) — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../security/BasicAuthenticationConfig.java`: `@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled=true)` (line 19, this is what activates `@PreAuthorize`), CSRF disabled, `anyRequest().authenticated()`, HTTP Basic; JDBC authentication querying `users`/`roles` tables.
- `DisableSecurityConfig` (`...enable=false`) — CSRF disabled, `anyRequest().permitAll()`, no `@EnableMethodSecurity`.

Important: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/application.properties` line 49 sets `petclinic.security.enable=false` by default. So in the default profile `DisableSecurityConfig` loads, method security is NOT enabled, and the `@PreAuthorize` is effectively inert (all requests permitted). Only when security is enabled is `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` enforced.

`ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleAccessDeniedException` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/.../rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java` lines 84-87) re-throws `AccessDeniedException` so Security produces a 403 (authenticated, wrong role) rather than a 500.

## 7. Event publishing / logging / email / other side-effects

- No event publishing (`ApplicationEventPublisher`/`@EventListener`), no email/`JavaMailSender`, no messaging anywhere in the create path.
- Logging: none in the controller/service happy path. The only logging is in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` (SLF4J), and only on error: `handleGeneralException` logs `error` (500); `handleDataIntegrityViolationException` logs `warn`+`debug` (mapped to 404); `handleMethodArgumentNotValidException` logs `debug` (400). Validation failures of the `@Valid` body surface as `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 with a ProblemDetail listing invalid fields.
- Data side-effects during a successful create: writes to the `owners` table (new row) and possible UPDATEs to existing owners' `household_id` when joining a household (`assignHousehold` back-fill).

---

## Exact order of validations and side-effects

1. HTTP request hits the security filter chain. If security enabled: HTTP Basic authentication, then `anyRequest().authenticated()`. If disabled (default): permitAll.
2. Method-level authorization (only when security enabled / `@EnableMethodSecurity` active): `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` requires `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`; failure → 403.
3. Request body deserialized to `OwnerFieldsDto`; `@Valid` triggers Bean Validation on the DTO BEFORE the controller body: `@NotNull`, `@Size`, `@Pattern` on firstName/lastName/address/city; `@NotNull @Size` plus custom `@TelephoneValidation` (→ `E164Telephone.isValid`) on telephone; `@Size @Email` on email if present. Any failure → `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 (no service/DB calls happen).
4. Controller body begins. `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` maps and normalizes: address (`AddressNormalizer`), telephone (`E164Telephone.normalize`), email (lowercase). id/pets/householdId/namesakeCount are not set.
5. `BusinessDays.effectiveRegistrationDate(...)` computes the effective registration date (default now, rolled off weekends) and sets it on the owner.
6. Daily capacity check: `countOwnersRegisteredOn(effectiveDate) >= 100` → 429 Too Many Requests (short-circuits).
7. Telephone uniqueness: `isTelephoneInUse(normalizedTelephone)` → 409 Conflict.
8. City capacity: `countOwnersInCity(city) >= 50` → 409 Conflict.
9. Household check: `isHouseholdInUse(lastName, address)`. If a household already exists AND `sharesHousehold != true` → 409 Conflict. If it exists AND `sharesHousehold == true` → `assignHousehold(owner)` sets the owner's `householdId` and back-fills/saves existing members.
10. `owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(firstName, lastName))`.
11. `saveOwner(owner)`: if `customerCode` is null, generate `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`; then `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.
12. During persist/flush, JPA fires the `@PrePersist onCreate()` callback (re-applies the business-day registration-date policy; idempotent) plus entity-level Bean Validation on `Owner`/`Person` constraints.
13. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` builds the response, computing derived fields (displayName, initials, membershipNumber, membershipTier, locality).
14. `Location` header set to `/api/owners/{id}`; respond `201 Created` with the `OwnerDto`.

Errors thrown anywhere are translated by `ExceptionControllerAdvice` (400 for validation, 404 for data-integrity, 403 for access-denied, 500 otherwise), with logging only on those error paths.
